--- Cut levels --------
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.MinAccumLevelToSave = -1 >   // minimum accum level to save the event

--- Systematics ------------

The single systematics configuration (when EnableSingle...SystConfigurations = 0)
or the all systematics configuration (when EnableAllSystematics = 0)
need to be enabled in baseAnalysis parameter file

--- Corrections -----------
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.ApplySCECorrection = 1 >

--- Systematics ------------
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.ApplySCESystematic = 0 >

--- Event Display ------------
 # Event display data is always saved to EventDisplayData tree for signal candidates.
 # This allows regeneration with full OpenGL zoom via DrawingTools::EvtDisplay()
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.CreateEventDisplay = 1 >

--- Annihilation Vertex Finder ------------
# Pairing: max distance between RECONSTRUCTED track start positions (PositionStart). In LArTPC these are
# often the first hit on each track, NOT the true decay point, so two pions from the same K0 can have
# "starts" 20-50 cm apart. Use a loose value here; the real cut is AnnihilationVertexMaxClosestApproach.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.AnnihilationVertexRadius = 50.0 >
# Quality: max distance of closest approach (cm) of the two track lines at the vertex. True K0->pipi
# decay has both tracks meeting at one point; we require the extrapolated tracks to come this close.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.AnnihilationVertexMaxClosestApproach = 5.0 >

--- Creation Vertex Finder ------
< neutralKaonAnalysis.CreationVertexRadius = 20.0 > //distance threshold (cm) for creation vertex sphere radius; larger to find proton when beam end is misreconstructed
< neutralKaonAnalysis.CreationVertexRadiusAlongBeam = 50.0 > //when matching secondaries to beam line (not only beam end), max distance (cm) to line; increase to recover proton when beam end is misreconstructed
< neutralKaonAnalysis.CreationMaxDistanceFromBeamEnd = 50.0 > //max distance (cm) of creation vertex from beam end along beam; K0 is created where beam stops, not in the middle of the beam track
< neutralKaonAnalysis.MinCreationAnnihilationSeparation = 5.0 > //min separation (cm) between creation and annihilation vertices; reject pairs below this to avoid track confusion

These variables below are unused as the framework uses Pandora-based
quantities to extrapolate lines and find vertices

< neutralKaonAnalysis.VertexFindingMethod = 0 > //vertex position finding method: 0=Geometric(PCA), 1=Fitted(TMinuit-default), 2=Kalman
< neutralKaonAnalysis.MaxKalmanChi2Ndf = 10.0 > //max chi2/ndf for Kalman vertex fit quality (vertices with higher values are rejected)
< neutralKaonAnalysis.UsePandora = 0 > // Use Pandora-based vertex (1) or Fit-based vertex (0) for general variables

--- Filter vertices (one particle per vertex) ---
# FilterVerticesByScore keeps vertices in order of effective score; each particle can appear in at most one vertex.
# FilterVerticesFavourGeometry = 1: add penalties for large opening angle, short min-daughter length, low min-daughter nhits
#   (based on signal vs background diagnostics: signal has smaller opening, longer daughters, more hits).
# FilterVerticesFavourTwoPions = 1: add mass near K0 + pion PID terms (weak when background is also pi+ pi-; use with care).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FilterVerticesFavourGeometry = 1 > // 1 = favour small opening angle, long daughters, many hits; use small weights to avoid efficiency loss
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FilterVerticesOpeningAngleWeight = 0.005 > // penalty per degree (try 0.002–0.01; too large can reduce efficiency)
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FilterVerticesMinDaughterLengthWeight = 0.01 > // penalty per cm below threshold
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FilterVerticesMinDaughterLengthThreshold = 40.0 > // cm
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FilterVerticesMinDaughterNhitsWeight = 0.002 > // penalty per hit below threshold
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FilterVerticesMinDaughterNhitsThreshold = 50.0 > // collection-plane hits
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FilterVerticesFavourTwoPions = 0 > // 1 = also add mass + pion PID terms; 0 recommended (weak discriminator)
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FilterVerticesK0MassWeight = 1e-5 > // weight for (M_pipi - M_K0)^2 term (MeV^-2)
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FilterVerticesPionChi2Weight = 0.01 > // weight for max(chi2/ndf_pion) of the two tracks

--- Neutral Particle Scoring ----
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.CylinderRadius = 7.5 >
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.ImpactParameter = 0.0 > //selection level

--- Alternative Annihilation Vertex Finding Parameters (not used) -----------
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.TrackFitLength = 5.0 > //length of track used for line fitting (cm)
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.TrackFitMinDistance = 0.0 > //min distance from vertex (cm): use only hits in [TrackFitMinDistance, TrackFitLength] for line fit (0=no trim)

--- Creation Vertex Fit Parameters (optional overrides; if not set, fall back to TrackFitLength/TrackFitMinDistance) -----------
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.CreationTrackFitLength = 15.0 > //length of track used for creation vertex line fitting (cm)
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.CreationTrackFitMinDistance = 1.0 > //min distance for creation vertex: use only hits in [CreationTrackFitMinDistance, CreationTrackFitLength] from beam end / second start (cm)
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.CreationMinOpeningAngleCos = 0.98 > //cos(angle): if beam-second cos >= this, use midpoint of beam end and second start (nearly parallel fallback)
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.UseROOTFitting = 1 > //use ROOT fitting instead of PCA for track fitting (1=ROOT, 0=PCA)

--- Other Parameters -----------

--- Other Parameters -----------

--- Event Skim File ------------
 < baseAnalysis.StoreSurvivingEvents = 0 >  // Enable storing surviving events (0=disabled, 1=enabled)
 < baseAnalysis.TruthPDGForSkim = -1 >    // PDG code to check in truth (-1=disabled, e.g., 310 for K0)

###############################################################################
  baseAnalysis parameters
###############################################################################

This ia a copy of the baseAnalysis parameters file in highland, such that we can overwrite them


Whether to initialize trees or not at the beginning of each configuration

 < baseAnalysis.InitializeTrees = 1 >

 --- Corrections ------------

Disables all corrections regardless of the ones enabled below

 < baseAnalysis.Corrections.DisableAllCorrections  = 0 >

Apply all corrections even if they were already applied in the input file

 < baseAnalysis.Corrections.ForceApplyCorrections  = 0 >

Enable/Disable individual corrections


--- Event Weights ------------

Enable/disable configurations with a single systematic (when EnableSingleWeightSystConfigurations = 1)
and enable systematics in the "all_syst" configuration (when EnableAllSystematics = 1)

No weights yet !!!

--- Systematics ------------

Number of toy experiments
 < baseAnalysis.Systematics.NumberOfToys = 100 >

The Random Seed. When throwing toys we want the same random numbers for all jobs. Thus, the random seed should be the same in all cases (and different from 0 !!!!)

     0 --> A pure random seed is generated based on time
 not 0 --> A fix random seed is used

 < baseAnalysis.Systematics.RandomSeed = 1 >

Use a different random generator for each systematic

 < baseAnalysis.Systematics.IndividualRandomGenerator = 0 >


--- Configurations ------------

Create configurations with a single systematic ( a configuration for each systematic selected above)

 < baseAnalysis.Configurations.EnableSingleVariationSystConfigurations = 0 >
 < baseAnalysis.Configurations.EnableSingleWeightSystConfigurations    = 0 >

Enable/disable the configuration with all systematics (or the ones selected above)

 < baseAnalysis.Configurations.EnableAllSystematics = 0 >